<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.170 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.170 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due October 2 was 3.170 percent, up from 2.861 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.2 billion of 180-day T-bills due December 30 was 3.515 percent, up from 3.182 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 357-day T-bills due June 25, 1998 was 4.013 percent, up from 3.670 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$525 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$625 million of C$4.6 billion bills due July 10. (Details follow)  </p>
